This crate (`symphonia-codec-ra`) is a pure-Rust RealAudio 1.0 (14.4K) and RealAudio 2.0 (28.8K)
decoder. It is licensed under the Mozilla Public License, v. 2.0, like the rest of Project Symphonia.

Neither codec has a public specification. The algorithms and tables follow FFmpeg's
`libavcodec/ra144dec.c`, `libavcodec/ra144.c`, `libavcodec/ra144.h` (RealAudio 1.0), and
`libavcodec/ra288.c`, `libavcodec/ra288.h`, `libavcodec/g728_template.c`,
`libavcodec/lpc_functions.h`, `libavcodec/celp_filters.c` (RealAudio 2.0, a G.728 LD-CELP variant,
see ITU-T G.728 blocks 36, 46-49). The tables in `src/tables144.rs` and `src/tables288.rs` were
extracted programmatically from those files. FFmpeg's code is distributed under the GNU Lesser
General Public License, version 2.1 or later. FFmpeg's RealAudio 1.0 decoder is in turn based on the
public domain decoder at http://www.honeypot.net/audio.

